From 794ec3a2fce4c5625136bc3e28a0cbee8d327162 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:45:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): reuse one kept-alive Board-service
 connection per thread instead of a TLS handshake per request [daveey]

Hub._call opened a fresh urlopen connection for every Board-service request, so each paid a TCP connect, a TLS
handshake and a platform trust evaluation (truststore -> SecTrustEvaluateWithError on macOS). On David-MBP the
gateway's sync executor thread did ~3.6 handshakes/s while cards ran (36 SecTrustEvaluate in a 10 s sample).
Live replay against the real Board service through the gateway runtime: 10.1 ms thread-CPU per request with urlopen,
0.69 ms on a reused connection.

Hub now keeps one HTTP/1.1 connection per thread (fork-safe), drops it when the server closed it, after 30 s idle or on
Connection: close, and retries a GET once on a stale reused socket. A POST whose answer was lost is never resent.
Errors keep urlopen's contract (HubError/Resync for non-2xx, URLError for transport and protocol failures, which
http.client's BadStatusLine was not before). An environment proxy keeps the urlopen path.
